{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES-REQUESTED at exact clean head 68c0f42fee192e24bc194ec262cad359e4784fd3. I did not exercise the unauthorized public side effect.\n\n1. Outbound is not separately chartered by construction. --propose passes through the same charterIsLive/charterBinds check as observation, and that body checks only connector, owner, repo, and actor. Any live inbound charter with those four fields therefore authorizes opening a pull request; the code cannot distinguish the separately chartered outbound permission the package comments and request require. Require an explicit operation/direction (for example propose/outbound) and refuse a read-only charter on the write path. The missing operator charter is therefore not merely an unmet dogfood condition: the current implementation has no shape that can express and enforce it.\n\n2. The claimed marker defense is not connected. Owned is referenced only by render tests, never by List, Number, Fetch, or any inbound path. TestRenderThenReObserveProducesNoNewAct passes solely because pull_request is present. Remove that field and the connector ingests its own marker-bearing body. Either wire Owned into every inbound body path and make the end-to-end test independently kill both defenses, or remove the marker/“excluded twice” claim and rely honestly on pull-request exclusion.\n\n3. The command checks only that request, artifact, and commit strings are nonempty. It never verifies that the request and artifact exist and are effective, that the artifact commits exactly --commit, or that its provenance belongs to the governing request. It can therefore create an irreversible public rendering that confidently names mutually inconsistent durable facts—the case its own comment says it must refuse. Validate the exact projected request/artifact/head relationship before POST. Also require a positive issue number and a nonempty created html_url; a response with {number:7} currently prints success with no usable evidence URL.\n\n4. The existing connector contract still says Render “only overwrites a surface the connector owns,” both in internal/connector/github/observe.go and docs/concepts/connectors.md. This head instead opens a non-idempotent, non-overwritable pull request and explains the change only in new code. Update and re-anchor the behavior documentation so readers are not taught the opposite operational model.\n\n5. Artifact 4eb2dc81 has succession_unrecorded at internal/connector; retire live predecessor 2955bb97 for merged inbound head 0ad55599 with the successor as basis before re-review.\n\nWhat is sound: live/ratified/stale/retired charter checks do gate all execution; the rendered body names the supplied identifiers and places authority in gitseq; GitHub failure statuses are errors; the PR exclusion in both list and number reads prevents current PR read-back. Focused connector/cmd tests and go vet pass, diff/check and worktree are clean, and main merges cleanly at tree 17a75a99d907f730ab86ebca3d555bfc9b75d044.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:4eb2dc81fd837b4cd7e3ad5b8aeaf21e096ff12e","head":"68c0f42fee192e24bc194ec262cad359e4784fd3","verdict":"changes-requested"}}